# Hash-gated build inputs must keep LF endings on every platform. build.rs and the
# plugin build compute SHA-256 over these sources and compare against committed
# manifests (cuda/POM_FATBIN_MANIFEST.md, plugins/cuda/resources/PTX_MANIFEST.txt).
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts LF->CRLF (autocrlf) and the source hash
# no longer matches the manifest, failing the build ("committed walk image/source do
# not match"). Force LF for the CUDA/PTX sources and treat the fatbin as binary.
*.cu   text eol=lf
*.cuh  text eol=lf
*.ptx  text eol=lf
*.fatbin binary
# llama.cpp patches are applied byte-for-byte at build time (CMake / build scripts): never convert line endings.
tools/keryx-llama/patches/*.patch -text
